From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mzak <mzak.amin@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 23 Nov 2026 20:31:28 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] soc: qcom: smp2p_sleepstate: ignore sensor stream edges
 during suspend

Every system suspend that uses the /sys/power/wakeup_count handshake
(KDE's powerdevil before each suspend, our s2idle test row) is aborted
with "Some devices failed to suspend, or early wake event detected"
about 0.5 s after it starts, while a plain write to /sys/power/state
suspends fine.

While a sensor streams (the cover detector keeps proximity and
magnetometer at 5 Hz), the ADSP toggles the sleepstate_see entry at the
sample rate: a trace shows the smp2p-adsp interrupt every 200 ms, in
phase before, during and after a suspend attempt, also after
PM_SUSPEND_PREPARE has cleared the AP-awake bit. Since
commit a5b885ae8022 ("soc: qcom: smp2p_sleepstate: wakeup events only
while suspending"), every such edge between PM_SUSPEND_PREPARE and
PM_POST_SUSPEND is a wakeup event. The first one comes at most one
sample period after the notifier, before the devices are suspended; it
changes the wakeup event count saved by the handshake, so
pm_wakeup_pending() aborts the suspend.

Remember when the previous edge came. An edge within 2 s of the
previous one belongs to a running stream and is not reported; an edge
after a quiet period is still a wakeup event while a suspend is in
progress, as before. Outside a suspend nothing is reported, so a read
of /sys/power/wakeup_count still does not block while sensors stream.

Fixes: a5b885ae8022 ("soc: qcom: smp2p_sleepstate: wakeup events only while suspending")
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Signed-off-by: mzak <mzak.amin@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/soc/qcom/smp2p_sleepstate.c | 22 +++++++++++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 21 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/soc/qcom/smp2p_sleepstate.c b/drivers/soc/qcom/smp2p_sleepstate.c
index 139a465a41737..2c3716eb104fd 100644
--- a/drivers/soc/qcom/smp2p_sleepstate.c
+++ b/drivers/soc/qcom/smp2p_sleepstate.c
@@ -8,6 +8,7 @@
  * needs the AP-awake indication during suspend and resume.
  */
 #include <linux/interrupt.h>
+#include <linux/ktime.h>
 #include <linux/module.h>
 #include <linux/of.h>
 #include <linux/of_irq.h>
@@ -20,11 +21,20 @@
 #define PROC_AWAKE_ID	12
 #define AWAKE_BIT	BIT(PROC_AWAKE_ID)
 
+/*
+ * While a sensor streams, the DSP toggles the inbound entry at the sample
+ * rate (every 200 ms for a 5 Hz stream), with or without the AP-awake bit.
+ * An edge that comes within this time of the previous one belongs to such
+ * a stream.
+ */
+#define STREAM_GAP_MS	2000
+
 struct smp2p_sleepstate {
 	struct qcom_smem_state *state;
 	struct wakeup_source *ws;
 	struct notifier_block pm_nb;
 	bool suspending;
+	ktime_t last_edge;
 };
 
 static int smp2p_sleepstate_pm_notifier(struct notifier_block *nb,
@@ -49,6 +59,11 @@ static int smp2p_sleepstate_pm_notifier(struct notifier_block *nb,
 static irqreturn_t smp2p_sleepstate_handler(int irq, void *data)
 {
 	struct smp2p_sleepstate *ss = data;
+	ktime_t now = ktime_get();
+	bool stream = ktime_ms_delta(now, ss->last_edge) < STREAM_GAP_MS;
+
+	/* Only this threaded handler accesses last_edge */
+	ss->last_edge = now;
 
 	/*
 	 * Only a suspend in progress needs to hear that the DSP wants the AP
@@ -57,8 +72,13 @@ static irqreturn_t smp2p_sleepstate_handler(int irq, void *data)
 	 * edge kept the source active all the time, and a read of
 	 * /sys/power/wakeup_count blocks while any source is active (KDE's
 	 * powerdevil waited 25 s before every suspend).
+	 *
+	 * A running stream does not stop when the AP-awake bit is cleared, so
+	 * its edges are expected during a suspend as well: reported, the first
+	 * of them aborted every suspend that uses the wakeup_count handshake.
+	 * Only an edge after a quiet period is a request to stay awake.
 	 */
-	if (READ_ONCE(ss->suspending))
+	if (READ_ONCE(ss->suspending) && !stream)
 		__pm_wakeup_event(ss->ws, 200);
 
 	return IRQ_HANDLED;
-- 
2.43.0

